On Thu, 19 Oct 2006, Justin Hiltscher wrote:
> azgor wrote:
>> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
>> freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.
>> 
>> [1]: If some living foo creature is hit with turn-undead, it should
>> turn undead (ie. turn into a zombie foo). --azgor

   Contrary to people's objections here, this idea wouldn't necessarily
require a zombie monster for each monster type; it could just involve
adding a "zombified" flag to the monster struct. Still, I think it's
way too powerful a change --- the player shouldn't be able to zombify
everything he sees, even if that /doesn't/ give any real advantage.
(And it should; zombies are slow and stupid.) It's just too weird.

>> [2]: Rings of regeneration can have an enchantment - the higher the
>> enchantment the more it regenerates per turn and the more nutrition it
>> uses. Negatively enchanted rings sap your life to fill your belly
>> (doubly dangerous - death by choking or by life drain.) --Grunt
>> 
>> [3]: Wand of inversion a la Beyond Zork: turn containers and creatures
>> temporarily inside out, expelling their contents --aioli

   I think this is a really cool idea, now that I've thought of a
good general use for it; see the second bullet point below.

     * Instakill of non-resisting monsters (except bjvF), which implies
       charged wands should be as rare as /oD
     * Or, on second thought --- combine this YANI with the recent YANI
       about shuffling monsters, and make zapping a /oInv at a line of
       monsters reverse their ordering. Don't want to fight that ettin
       right now? Swap it for the hill orc at the other end of the hall!
       (Zapping at a single monster could still be an instakill, or
       could just act as confusion.)
     * Fun with containers, including cursed bags of holding and
       bags of tricks
     * Fun with purple worms
     * Silly (or really desperate) way to get out of a vortex
     * Yet another unique death
     * Bad pun: zap it at a tourist/sink/scroll of mail and get "Yep,
       there are ____s in this version!" :)
     * Possibly worse pun: zap it at a fortune cookie for a reversal
       of fortune

